{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: reordered the model-block sampling statements so that hyperparameters (`mu_alpha`, `sigma_alpha`, `mu_beta`, `sigma_beta`) receive their priors before they are used in the priors for `alpha` and `beta`. This preserves the same posterior/log density because Stan sampling statements add commutatively to the log density. The data file is unchanged.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=1> N;
  int<lower=1> J; // number of counties
  array[N] int<lower=1, upper=J> county;
  vector[N] u;
  vector[N] x;
  vector[N] y;
}
transformed data {
  matrix[N, 2] cov = [x', u']';
}
parameters {
  real mu_alpha;
  real mu_beta;
  real<lower=0> sigma;
  real<lower=0> sigma_alpha;
  real<lower=0> sigma_beta;
  vector<offset=mu_alpha, multiplier=sigma_alpha>[J] alpha;
  vector<offset=mu_beta, multiplier=sigma_beta>[2] beta;
}
model {
  mu_alpha ~ std_normal();
  sigma_alpha ~ cauchy(0, 2.5);
  mu_beta ~ std_normal();
  sigma_beta ~ cauchy(0, 2.5);
  sigma ~ cauchy(0, 2.5);
  alpha ~ normal(mu_alpha, sigma_alpha);
  beta ~ normal(mu_beta, sigma_beta);

  y ~ normal_id_glm(cov, alpha[county], beta, sigma);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"J":4,"N":3,"county":[1,1,1],"u":[6.8047718459683955,6.517974586272288,4.092786616976351],"x":[2.6500289313002243,3.215598354224198,4.819112710186972],"y":[3.0,3.0,3.0]}","protected_variables":["y"]}
